{
  "helena|Between you and me, Liz? That boy is your other half. Everyone can see it but you.": "audio/voice/helena-6676bfecff.mp3",
  "helena|I found a box of your mom's things in the pantry. I thought maybe we could look through it together?": "audio/voice/helena-8883f588a1.mp3",
  "helena|I'm never going to replace her, Liz. I just want to know you.": "audio/voice/helena-89482e04ca.mp3",
  "helena|Liz, honey, is that Wes's hoodie? It looks cute on you.": "audio/voice/helena-57211e9bde.mp3",
  "helena|Never. Oh, and the frame on our family photo broke. Will you two help me put it back together?": "audio/voice/helena-93d02ccc66.mp3",
  "helena|Thank you for taking care of her, Wes. Really.": "audio/voice/helena-8d02dd8f3e.mp3",
  "helena|Your mom will always be your mom, Liz. I just want a spot in the picture too.": "audio/voice/helena-c60fb012ee.mp3",
  "jocelyn|Hmm. That's not her. Try again, Bennett.": "audio/voice/jocelyn-eafd5a2bfe.mp3",
  "jocelyn|Okay, Bennett. I see you. You actually get her.": "audio/voice/jocelyn-f4fd8527c4.mp3",
  "jocelyn|So are you two, like, a thing now?": "audio/voice/jocelyn-d3613de2fc.mp3",
  "jocelyn|You have my blessing. Don't make me regret it.": "audio/voice/jocelyn-43d8e993d2.mp3",
  "liz-kid|*opens the little library* ...AAAAAH! Its HEAD! Where is the rest of it?!": "audio/voice/liz-kid-678d39e084.mp3",
  "liz-kid|EWWW! There is a FROG in my Dreamhouse! WESLEY BENNETT!": "audio/voice/liz-kid-2075888f30.mp3",
  "liz-kid|That is NOT how the movie goes.": "audio/voice/liz-kid-dfb78467be.mp3",
  "liz|I can't do this right now.": "audio/voice/liz-a4581f6b66.mp3",
  "liz|I didn't have to be anybody else tonight. Thanks, Wes.": "audio/voice/liz-a0ff8cc1c1.mp3",
  "liz|I know. I think… I think she would've liked you.": "audio/voice/liz-78e11871dc.mp3",
  "liz|Is it bad? Tell me the truth.": "audio/voice/liz-f04b8d6751.mp3",
  "liz|It's the three of us. It feels like if I'm in the picture, I'm erasing her.": "audio/voice/liz-7ec1c6653c.mp3",
  "liz|Just shut up and kiss me.": "audio/voice/liz-843a6f75c8.mp3",
  "liz|Okay, that heart is actually adorable. Who knew Wes Bennett was an artist?": "audio/voice/liz-92e37d26b9.mp3",
  "liz|Okay. New plan. What if we pretend to date? You talk me up, Michael gets jealous, and I finally get my moment.": "audio/voice/liz-1a0340a473.mp3",
  "liz|She kept Mom's teacup. On the top shelf. I thought she'd thrown it all away.": "audio/voice/liz-ad5d2f41ca.mp3",
  "liz|Ten rounds and not a scratch. Did you see that, Michael?": "audio/voice/liz-2ae99096e2.mp3",
  "liz|Thanks, Wes. This is the worst night of my life.": "audio/voice/liz-48bb7d1799.mp3",
  "liz|Those are hers. You can't just… go through her stuff.": "audio/voice/liz-e50a374404.mp3",
  "liz|Wait, what blessing? Joss, what are you talking about?": "audio/voice/liz-db8eae607f.mp3",
  "liz|Wes, who ARE you right now? This feels like a movie set.": "audio/voice/liz-a733b0d810.mp3",
  "liz|Wes? It's pouring! What are you doing out here?": "audio/voice/liz-c7db22cfc2.mp3",
  "liz|Wes…": "audio/voice/liz-1402fe9783.mp3",
  "liz|What? No! I mean… it's complicated. Don't ask.": "audio/voice/liz-a5c1b25c04.mp3",
  "liz|You know what? You treated me exactly like you always do.": "audio/voice/liz-f64552de2b.mp3",
  "michael|Liz? Was that you who got puked on? Rough.": "audio/voice/michael-cd2ca5664a.mp3",
  "michael|Nice moves, Liz.": "audio/voice/michael-a1d9b3488b.mp3",
  "michael|You guys coming? Movie's starting.": "audio/voice/michael-a502300f88.mp3",
  "narrator|It's better than the movies.": "audio/voice/narrator-f5ebc88a89.mp3",
  "narrator|Libby always waited for the grand romantic gestures, the kind she grew up watching in rom-coms.": "audio/voice/narrator-f6a35f5990.mp3",
  "narrator|Libby thought about what he said all night.": "audio/voice/narrator-5817865f5a.mp3",
  "narrator|Ten years later…": "audio/voice/narrator-8fbb6647e2.mp3",
  "narrator|That night in the parking spot, Liz finally realized that Wes, not Michael, was her real-life Mark Darcy.": "audio/voice/narrator-437413ee20.mp3",
  "narrator|True love isn't like the movies. It's messy, and it's built on communication, trust, and being brave enough to be vulnerable.": "audio/voice/narrator-3dc2dc72d7.mp3",
  "narrator|Wes found the hidden Chuck Taylors! Equip them to move at double speed.": "audio/voice/narrator-edb52c826b.mp3",
  "narrator|What she never noticed were the small ones. The spare clothes. The rides to the hospital. A car window closed in the rain.": "audio/voice/narrator-658131f7ce.mp3",
  "noah|OH NO. Liz, I am so sorry!": "audio/voice/noah-7d8e1ece4e.mp3",
  "wes-kid|Come on, little guy. Barbie's waiting. Try again!": "audio/voice/wes-kid-bfb8c910f8.mp3",
  "wes-kid|He just wanted a kiss from Barbie. Like the movie!": "audio/voice/wes-kid-0517d2483e.mp3",
  "wes-kid|It's a guardian gnome. He guards your books. With his face.": "audio/voice/wes-kid-93f247fddb.mp3",
  "wes-kid|They are too fast! One more try.": "audio/voice/wes-kid-e4cd221797.mp3",
  "wes|A puzzle? Please. Bennett's got this.": "audio/voice/wes-05fae6a3c2.mp3",
  "wes|About ten years after the frog and gnome scandal, Liz needed my help. Liz always had a thing for a boy named Michael, who moved out of our neighborhood a few years back. Once he finally moved back, Liz wanted to make her move.": "audio/voice/wes-48f774ec39.mp3",
  "wes|After I renewed Libby's wardrobe for Michael, I picked her up to take her to a basketball game where Michael would meet us.": "audio/voice/wes-a9a3bd12e1.mp3",
  "wes|After Michael made a comment about thinking Libby's 'cute dress' was a uniform, I wanted to make it up to her. I decided to take her to the mall to step up her wardrobe.": "audio/voice/wes-0d972d156b.mp3",
  "wes|As you could imagine, giving a little girl a severed gnome head might not have been the best way to go.": "audio/voice/wes-2be988f425.mp3",
  "wes|But this story is not hers. It is mine.": "audio/voice/wes-ab5182dbb1.mp3",
  "wes|Chuck Taylors. With a note: 'For the boy next door. You deserve a pair too. —Liz'": "audio/voice/wes-625cc3a86b.mp3",
  "wes|Fake-dating Liz Buxbaum. What could possibly go wrong?": "audio/voice/wes-c2ae06abb8.mp3",
  "wes|Helena isn't trying to replace her mom. She just wants to be her friend.": "audio/voice/wes-7add3d442f.mp3",
  "wes|Here. Sweats and my hoodie. They're clean, I swear.": "audio/voice/wes-ae9a9a6eec.mp3",
  "wes|I decided to take this as a small step towards my ultimate goal: win over Libby's heart.": "audio/voice/wes-0fa3e91561.mp3",
  "wes|I didn't consider that she might feel a sense of disgust toward the little creatures.": "audio/voice/wes-0d3cd4eb1f.mp3",
  "wes|I don't want to say that I was happy with the outcome, but at least she didn't have her moment with Michael, and instead it gave me the opportunity to give her an extra pair of clothes.": "audio/voice/wes-b2f9b5b9e0.mp3",
  "wes|I feel like I'd do anything just to get her gaze up at me the way she does.": "audio/voice/wes-20ad3961cb.mp3",
  "wes|I have loved Libby since the second grade, when I realized that I could turn her cheeks pink with just a word.": "audio/voice/wes-7ee3675aa2.mp3",
  "wes|I joined her and we both had a great time before going to Michael's house for a movie. I hope this will help show her that I am the one for her.": "audio/voice/wes-49a9c2b049.mp3",
  "wes|I just didn't want your moldy car ruining the property value of the whole neighborhood, Buxbaum.": "audio/voice/wes-25cf22d492.mp3",
  "wes|I took Liz to her favorite restaurant, and in my opinion the best burger place in town, Stella's.": "audio/voice/wes-c14301035c.mp3",
  "wes|I tried to make up for the frog incident by gifting Libby a guardian gnome for her little neighborhood library.": "audio/voice/wes-5b19d0c9f7.mp3",
  "wes|I want to show Liz that the only way for her to grow is to accept that she can't hold tightly onto past memories just to avoid the pain of the present.": "audio/voice/wes-f0dab91326.mp3",
  "wes|I was planning on telling her that I have been in love with her since the second grade, when I realized her eyes are the most beautiful things I've ever seen.": "audio/voice/wes-c8f6bc8b1d.mp3",
  "wes|I would tell her how much I love the way her eyes transform whenever she talks about music, or how she's the type of funny that makes you want to spit out your drink.": "audio/voice/wes-54e5d8d2b2.mp3",
  "wes|I'm taking her to dinner, and I'm making sure it's not the Hollywood-perfect version she's expecting. No violins. No rose petals. Just us.": "audio/voice/wes-584497ce6a.mp3",
  "wes|I'm Wes Bennett, the boy next door. And I've been in love with Liz since the second grade.": "audio/voice/wes-07dd7c2ada.mp3",
  "wes|I've got you. Come on, we're going to the hospital.": "audio/voice/wes-316a523a2a.mp3",
  "wes|If Michael can't see that she's perfect just the way she is, that's his loss.": "audio/voice/wes-3a44a5d076.mp3",
  "wes|Ketchup is my medium. I'm very misunderstood.": "audio/voice/wes-1c4e9a3fc2.mp3",
  "wes|Liz and Helena don't get along easily, because Libby is afraid that if she becomes close with Helena, she will forget about her late mother.": "audio/voice/wes-d3e2e25855.mp3",
  "wes|Liz and I didn't end up going to homecoming together, but I still had a plan to win her over. I was waiting for her drive home so that I could make my move.": "audio/voice/wes-09502f1e2f.mp3",
  "wes|Liz and I wanted to go to Michael's house for a movie after her nose was fully healed, but we wanted to go to dinner first.": "audio/voice/wes-6b996bf611.mp3",
  "wes|Liz Buxbaum has always believed in rom-com love. She has been waiting her whole life for her own Mark Darcy, and she is pretty sure it is Michael.": "audio/voice/wes-f6ef23bb84.mp3",
  "wes|Liz has spent a lot of time and energy changing herself for her childhood crush instead of accepting herself.": "audio/voice/wes-c4ab5e1ede.mp3",
  "wes|Michael and I were invited to a party at my friend Ryno's house, and I was her ticket to having a moment with Michael after all these years.": "audio/voice/wes-9828eff1d1.mp3",
  "wes|My friend Noah tried passing the ball and ended up hitting Liz right in the nose. I quickly helped her up and took her to the hospital because her nose looked broken.": "audio/voice/wes-71b635798a.mp3",
  "wes|My palms are sweaty… I choked. One more shot.": "audio/voice/wes-176b1791a6.mp3",
  "wes|Nobody's taking anything, Liz. We'll just look. Together.": "audio/voice/wes-f89a818b38.mp3",
  "wes|Omaha, Nebraska. 2021.": "audio/voice/wes-f453a2d0ec.mp3",
  "wes|She has to drive to work early tomorrow morning. If I leave it, her seats will be soaked.": "audio/voice/wes-7d2e17e235.mp3",
  "wes|Show-off. Here, you earned my lucky cap.": "audio/voice/wes-90181643f0.mp3",
  "wes|Since her nose had swollen up, my friends and I got another awesome opportunity to tease Mrs. Potato Head.": "audio/voice/wes-092bf9d102.mp3",
  "wes|So I'm going out there. In the storm. For a car. That isn't even mine.": "audio/voice/wes-54879eb3c4.mp3",
  "wes|There's a thunderstorm, and I can see that Libby's car door window is wide open.": "audio/voice/wes-a9a1421963.mp3",
  "wes|There's something I need you to hear, Libby. Help me find the right words.": "audio/voice/wes-d9fa0cabc1.mp3",
  "wes|To find out how we got here, we have to go back about ten years…": "audio/voice/wes-56689cbcbd.mp3",
  "wes|Told you. I'm always right here, Buxbaum. Always.": "audio/voice/wes-4e99d8bf22.mp3",
  "wes|Too many people! Liz is still waiting. Try again.": "audio/voice/wes-23b733dd5f.mp3",
  "wes|Ugh, soaked. Let's try that again.": "audio/voice/wes-a3377bbd0f.mp3",
  "wes|Wait, what's this in the back of my car?": "audio/voice/wes-b843eb9591.mp3",
  "wes|We had just finished watching The Princess and the Frog in school when I came to the conclusion that Liz would love a frog in her Barbie Dreamhouse.": "audio/voice/wes-1ef9c8fa7f.mp3",
  "wes|We spent hours picking out outfits while I planned to surprise her with a new pair of Chuck Taylors.": "audio/voice/wes-042ffecb6b.mp3",
  "wes|What Liz didn't take into account was that we were going to a beer party, and that she might be the unlucky person to get barfed on.": "audio/voice/wes-9adda7cf8d.mp3",
  "wes|When the game ended, the boys and I decided to sneak into the gym and shoot some hoops. Everyone seemed to have a good time while I watched Liz flirt with Michael, until that turned into a huge mess.": "audio/voice/wes-3d749bdbb2.mp3",
  "wes|When we arrived, I asked Liz why she was writing her initials on a napkin with a heart around it in ketchup. She told me it was something she used to do in her childhood and begged me to do it as well, to go down memory lane.": "audio/voice/wes-515836f9b7.mp3",
  "wes|You look great, Mrs. Potato Head. Truly. A vision.": "audio/voice/wes-187522ef41.mp3"
}
